#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096394 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/id #uuid "f1021ccd-e37f-5880-baf2-0f0eacd7dd95" :question/math-academy-id "e-481" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096395 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "99b7b82d-431f-5992-9b1e-a80a6b3850c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-482" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "6269e793-cee7-59d6-8656-12a5a7475f2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-483" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/id #uuid "55a54d74-449e-5720-b808-9f275b678b2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-484" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29d1f345-a59a-5e1b-84c9-b73104f5f7ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288641} {:answer/id #uuid "458b8e3b-5d39-5c29-bcf9-1a0a521d544a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288642} {:answer/id #uuid "95aff211-caee-5146-aa0d-57382c1db850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288643} {:answer/id #uuid "fa44f4a2-4f42-5beb-858b-ff98c173a535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288644} {:answer/id #uuid "89434005-bb31-5102-b10d-8638d6f1abd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95aff211-caee-5146-aa0d-57382c1db850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288643} :answer-field/id #uuid "43cb7edd-f6c0-59ff-97a8-6a40eb18ee34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dc1619ed-6b5b-58ae-8fd5-aff3425b7d6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-10049" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096849 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a038f1d3-fd1c-5a25-a854-84ee139c9b17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\cos 2x - 5 + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093502} {:answer/id #uuid "175c4d9c-8b77-51df-93e9-3a9d2627a82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos 2x - 5x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093503} {:answer/id #uuid "3612f581-efc3-5949-b943-dd4cabb70a4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\cos 2x - 5x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093504} {:answer/id #uuid "52328aa8-f6fc-52ea-9e60-c67ab5bb8c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\cos 2x - 5x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093505} {:answer/id #uuid "662df38f-55e6-5818-a574-599928b3b854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\cos 2x - 5x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3612f581-efc3-5949-b943-dd4cabb70a4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\cos 2x - 5x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093504} :answer-field/id #uuid "4225b174-e4e9-5de3-8b24-d05d3f1140dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7507030-351a-513f-a28e-962e017050ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-10423" :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-5x+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c84c1bb4-91bc-5d3f-87bd-720d19a15f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288648} {:answer/id #uuid "2ad823bf-3426-5fa9-bca1-e4287658a589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288649} {:answer/id #uuid "58d0124e-76c0-5d05-ac2b-52ccd59034f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288650} {:answer/id #uuid "e25b4bbc-57f8-5b7a-9683-b6becf86a9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288651} {:answer/id #uuid "addb0da7-e313-5a86-a7b2-2c7da07e3afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "addb0da7-e313-5a86-a7b2-2c7da07e3afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288652} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b6b050b-db82-5654-aa4b-228df0c7bc4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "797afd23-724c-5bc8-886b-e0ec5110b301" :question/math-academy-id "q-114600" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41e225e4-2ee1-5814-a582-e6909c47e280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288655} {:answer/id #uuid "dac30b7c-f0b1-5d3a-9e2d-0068f819b118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288656} {:answer/id #uuid "110cffd9-5a80-5622-b762-451a6bea3517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288657} {:answer/id #uuid "2548ab99-eeff-5b0f-8013-ecbd30fee4f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288658} {:answer/id #uuid "6580d80e-f036-5373-be82-e21593775432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e225e4-2ee1-5814-a582-e6909c47e280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288655} :answer-field/id #uuid "e12514f3-672a-524d-80c8-c4ad7465c258" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b4ce5cf0-789a-541d-8352-d0ab9f8317eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-114681" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{5x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x]}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot [0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "305f1836-03a2-5996-ac20-2279b76dbedb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288662} {:answer/id #uuid "fe681a7f-808e-5856-9c3a-07c3ce8fc9ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288663} {:answer/id #uuid "b553eecb-871b-521a-a718-80f79c61cb0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288664} {:answer/id #uuid "53e74fc5-5f87-5c4f-aedb-372f9fb3ed7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288665} {:answer/id #uuid "e366eff6-8494-5906-8b37-c7aab76797ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe681a7f-808e-5856-9c3a-07c3ce8fc9ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288663} :answer-field/id #uuid "30338ea3-4603-5e3b-899d-40b67db48294" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bedb5f06-5e35-54a5-b2b1-195e60660069" :question/math-academy-id "q-114687" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (4-{cos}^{2}⁡4x+{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4-{cos}^{2}⁡4x+{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-[{cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x])\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4-\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a105aec-230b-517f-841c-b2661bf2a900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288669} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e3b438-1c73-56ac-9412-4592de70d7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288670} {:answer/id #uuid "d59678ce-a185-53af-be9a-c8d960acb4b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288671} {:answer/id #uuid "29ef0955-b526-5552-b399-ffcbc9567878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288672} {:answer/id #uuid "9c382ece-6e51-56d8-bce3-c4235b81f26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29ef0955-b526-5552-b399-ffcbc9567878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288672} :answer-field/id #uuid "557b5326-0b9a-5ce6-9ba9-59bb1ceaac8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "11ec7c4e-aed1-52ff-98e9-641fb20ec61b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114688" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25f1bf2-c930-5b22-a8db-5be2f26e0434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288676} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd147c6-56fd-5068-b331-75c40b883eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288677} {:answer/id #uuid "3e74b079-a2aa-52e8-9e8c-9ababc97c413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288678} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4eb8f2-67f0-5cc2-8d92-d698f00693a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288679} {:answer/id #uuid "36daac32-448e-5b89-bbe0-dcce889692b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c4eb8f2-67f0-5cc2-8d92-d698f00693a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288679} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b6ee84-c2ff-5008-a4a0-f6bf6d0c463b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42cfff07-e14f-55ef-a410-5b14971a6604" :question/math-academy-id "q-114691" :question/problem "$\\int 4{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdee7ed6-1a8f-54de-9565-51f219e60e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288683} {:answer/id #uuid "0c4da88e-6bf4-531e-ab90-288ecb0c94b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288684} {:answer/id #uuid "3667d8dd-62ef-5ca7-afca-c75934c792d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288685} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb0eec1-9fbf-51e8-a763-722a3bb144e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288686} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b0430a-1051-59f4-a4d3-becb03557c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3667d8dd-62ef-5ca7-afca-c75934c792d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288685} :answer-field/id #uuid "53e0cef4-4ec4-5875-8360-ecbadc3c00c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b05aee78-b1e6-53ea-9d88-ddd8ea7bedf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114712" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54a3427a-3ed4-5605-9c49-74f759bcf245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54a3427a-3ed4-5605-9c49-74f759bcf245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288690} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fcd1929-8fa5-5e11-9699-492206e5fe2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6aaa3cde-2f29-5bb8-a80e-dee5f4f375ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-347169" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ so letting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x))={sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,|}_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3}]-[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}] \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{5\\pi }{2}]-[0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a6e0165-9d83-55fb-ae2d-479f4739eeb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288693} {:answer/id #uuid "ac39ac42-f4e3-514b-9b2e-99f867283e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a6e0165-9d83-55fb-ae2d-479f4739eeb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288693} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d5ffffe-5e70-56f4-9655-682fd848b6fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "255b135e-4c97-5cce-be01-da73a642bcfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-348719" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de83bb90-abdb-5a3d-884a-69e3320c692f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de83bb90-abdb-5a3d-884a-69e3320c692f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288697} :answer-field/id #uuid "b92e5733-f6fc-5ad4-9465-bed23e133f28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "576f9457-846c-59f4-9d82-575b8b0af437" :question/math-academy-id "q-348727" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/0817984c94a989cc5d0801c829e9c0479c7afb30223450faea46ec486b4494c6.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+4x+7,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+4x+7)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(-5{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+5{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+4x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{x}^{2}+7x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2(0)^{2}+7\\cdot 0]-[-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+2{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+7(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =0-[5+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-\\frac{7\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =-5-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}+\\frac{7\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3f48758-89c7-542b-b1e8-2d24d6ddd394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^2+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3f48758-89c7-542b-b1e8-2d24d6ddd394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^2+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288700} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c460fe4-3716-512a-938e-1d14c7ed32b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2300b555-d4cf-537b-b3e9-89fb46a82bd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-348731" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/020a73150209de3ee6f95fa1b21c85bd5673e500e4e421459eff90d2dd1a42e9.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+2x+1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}+x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+(\\pi )^{2}+\\pi ]-[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+(0)^{2}+0] \\\\  & =[0+{\\pi }^{2}+\\pi ]-0 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}+\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3656a9ce-cf11-5425-954f-ceb2efe016c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288703} {:answer/id #uuid "84449871-191d-5637-94e3-a16b17deb5e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3656a9ce-cf11-5425-954f-ceb2efe016c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288703} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d8aabe-cca0-5e52-8aa9-01a82ce41369" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59621c1e-c337-504d-b5c3-072a2b288cb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-348737" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression $4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2.\n$$\n\nThus, the integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7ac88c6-2f61-5603-a45d-ae4315661c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288707} {:answer/id #uuid "74e9a655-be9a-5523-82a8-cf796f18cf77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7ac88c6-2f61-5603-a45d-ae4315661c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288707} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ed4fe93-90db-59f3-a3ee-5607fb98fe68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5d96771-5464-5364-b3e2-4d1ca6686960" :question/math-academy-id "q-348766" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/5e40f35729a8e3df9f8403cad85bf0c4e6045733616c86cc399548a901c03ac7.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)+x-1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dad7536-f9bc-5313-969e-801335ea608e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dad7536-f9bc-5313-969e-801335ea608e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288711} :answer-field/id #uuid "30240bdb-bbd2-5716-afdc-557f0ab92de2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9bec4b7b-50be-5186-a890-374f470de83e" :question/math-academy-id "q-348876" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/24f2892d622c6a28eb5f95a89f0e1ae7223b07e6219f50698ecef3d0c1c08e1a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve\n$y=2x-{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{2},$\nthe $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=2x-{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2},$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x-{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x-{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4}))-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{16}-\\frac{1}{4})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f1049f2-2eae-51be-889e-fbf7dbd882b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f1049f2-2eae-51be-889e-fbf7dbd882b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288714} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9f1742-a39a-54a0-831d-bb6189b2ee7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a363d9a1-7a76-54c0-adef-4dbfa47f4507" :question/math-academy-id "q-348884" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}[4{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{6})-2+4cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})]\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6}$, we have\n\n$$\n4{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{6})=2(1-cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,\\,[4{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{6})-2+4cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})]dx & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,\\,[2-2cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-2+4cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})\\,dx \\\\  & =6sin\\,(\\frac{x}{3}){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =6[sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{6})] \\\\  & =6(1-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0b43558-1ee5-5310-9696-7b724f0c24e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0b43558-1ee5-5310-9696-7b724f0c24e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288717} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c9ca8a7-11d7-5f7d-9bfe-dae53f87a97a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "96160f49-5771-5963-8f38-4fb3d428d104" :question/math-academy-id "q-361705" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x & =3{sin}^{2}⁡x+3{cos}^{2}⁡x+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[3+\\frac{4}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(5+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})]-[5\\cdot 0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+1]-[0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi +4}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c2051e-d3a9-542e-b91b-b967187b4b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288720} {:answer/id #uuid "6076c689-9724-5b5c-8880-41e25d47e139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288721} {:answer/id #uuid "25dd9646-6985-5207-99b1-39672c04701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288722} {:answer/id #uuid "2513f56e-cfb8-50ec-9324-9ed723f03de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288723} {:answer/id #uuid "16b1d295-584c-593e-be48-7dc47b822216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25dd9646-6985-5207-99b1-39672c04701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288722} :answer-field/id #uuid "699a7e15-8eb8-5462-a07f-e0c61c1cb570" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf4d3f7d-82a2-5f54-8ec5-c5a17c445cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-74400" :question/problem "$\\int 8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d0b2b8-6037-5e30-8c7e-dc875e31d807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288727} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd8c527-f2cf-5bcd-b204-b5e9811dfd6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288728} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc46874-f687-57e2-aaba-12c246abf376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288729} {:answer/id #uuid "67419508-3f81-53e7-9110-63ca99506a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288730} {:answer/id #uuid "848fb85e-72a1-5896-93c7-89c1071885f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30d0b2b8-6037-5e30-8c7e-dc875e31d807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288727} :answer-field/id #uuid "65c462af-9369-5e19-acfc-b87c6a056b59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b373498-84db-5708-b542-71c40a8177eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-74410" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa999982-5373-50ab-935f-e56d6d4ad648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288734} {:answer/id #uuid "0499cd2a-b347-5a0d-adc2-7a1b8d74b6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288735} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc2c24f-6f8f-54b4-8a4e-7cd35f418f4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288736} {:answer/id #uuid "81a057af-ac63-559b-a00e-8bdb2ea31e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288737} {:answer/id #uuid "e18c6906-428e-54e1-b6ce-1669faf1994c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0499cd2a-b347-5a0d-adc2-7a1b8d74b6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288735} :answer-field/id #uuid "3365d369-d802-512d-8991-0d0f3d53e755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b08fd801-71aa-5fa5-b286-cb30a092f7cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-74787" :question/problem "$\\int {cos}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡3x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cos}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{1}{2}x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
